WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.344
Raj: Our capacity guardrail protects twenty percent reserve. Alerts use forecast and remaining space.

2
00:00:07.344 --> 00:00:14.137
Lukas: Storage headroom must cover delivery lead time. Escalate if arrival risks that reserve.

3
00:00:14.137 --> 00:00:20.497
Priya: Who's picking this up for delivery? Raj owns confirmations by tomorrow, right?

4
00:00:20.497 --> 00:00:26.929
Anika: My action item is the capacity pilot. Evidence review is due in two weeks.

5
00:00:26.929 --> 00:00:34.994
Hannah: I'll check correctness and comparable load. Maybe campaign inputs change the acceptance range.

6
00:00:34.994 --> 00:00:42.938
Raj: Yes, I'll update high-growth projections tomorrow. The protected reserve isn't emergency spending permission.

7
00:00:42.938 --> 00:00:49.635
Lukas: I'll test larger-instance fallback this week. Production switching still needs separate approval.

8
00:00:49.635 --> 00:00:57.243
Priya: Okay, sharding stays research, not a commitment. We'll review staffing after distribution results.

9
00:00:57.243 --> 00:01:05.284
Hannah: Bring both monthly costs and engineering effort. A cheap quote can hide operational expense.

10
00:01:05.284 --> 00:01:11.980
Anika: So, close the loop in two weeks. No growth assumption becomes fact without evidence.

